# The C/F face-value delta gated per FACE — the gates of docs/amr_cf_flux_gate.md §10
#
# 2026-09-22, branch `cfgate`, host-openmp Release (GNU 14.2.0, Kokkos 5.1.1), 48-core host.
# BASE  = `main` at 2426ef4 (the row gate).  AFTER = cfgate at ffd8834 (the per-FACE gate).
# Both arms were run from the SAME scripts, on the same host, with OMP_NUM_THREADS as noted.
#
# The one-sentence rule: the quadratic C/F face value applies on a 2:1 sub-face iff BOTH incident
# cells are regular fluid (fluid && !cut), and that one predicate drives the divergence RHS, the
# ABC cell-gradient substitution and the advecting face field through one emitter, so that
# D_std(Δuf) ≡ Δ_cfDiv holds identically.


## Gates I / I' / F — rule (I) and the face divergence (tests/test_amr_face_field.cpp)

Mesh: refineToSdf(band=0) on BO({8,8,8}, lmax=2) = 32^3 fine, sphere R = (0.125·3/4π)^(1/3)·32 at
the centre, cf=1, 25 steps at presIters=30. band=0 puts the finest level ONLY where the surface
cuts, so the 2:1 interface coincides with the cut band — the configuration the gate exists for.
`cfCutFaces` is Flow.diagnostics.num_cf_cut_faces (the C/F census, §6.5).

                                              row gate (BASE)   face gate (AFTER)
  band=0, aperture, cf=1
    cfCutFaces                                      672               672
    ‖D_std(Δuf) − Δ_cfDiv‖₂   (gate I)          2.0190e-01        9.8797e-17     (ref 5.5e-01)
    divNormFace               (gate F)          2.0182e-01        1.9129e-12
    divNormL2 (cell field)                      5.6084e-01        5.6140e-01
  band=0, sampled ghost closure, cf=1
    ‖D_std(Δuf) − Δ_cfDiv‖₂                     2.3476e-01        1.0597e-16     (ref 5.5e-01)
    divNormFace over REGULAR fluid rows          4.9184e-13        2.7695e-13
    divNormL2 over REGULAR fluid rows           5.5584e-01        5.5727e-01
  band=3 (finest band), aperture, cf=1
    cfCutFaces                (gate C')                0                 0
    ‖D_std(Δuf) − Δ_cfDiv‖₂   (gate I')         1.0114e-16        1.0114e-16     unchanged

The note predicted 2.018e-01 / 2.016e-01 for the aperture band=0 pair; reproduced at
2.0190e-01 / 2.0182e-01. It also predicted the ghost path's REGULAR rows would carry "the
2e-1-class mismatch" before the change; they did not — that norm was already 4.9e-13. The sharp
instrument on the ghost path is the identity, which did carry it (2.3476e-01).


## Gate C — the census is an exact decomposition invariant (tests/test_amr_distributed_seam_mpi)

Σ_ranks numCfCutFaces(), WORLD vs a single-rank SELF build of the same octree:

  np = 1   96   (SELF 96)
  np = 2   96   (SELF 96)
  np = 4   96   (SELF 96)
  np = 8   96   (SELF 96)

The note predicted this mesh (a two-level latitude map ON the cut band) contains the
configuration. It does. tests/test_amr_distributed_cf_mpi's mesh is a uniformly finest band and
reports 0 on every rank, as it must.


