## Gate P — Z&H permeability against a uniform-fine reference

Recipe (the ROADMAP's "byte gate's own graded sphere": state_hash.py's sph, r=0.22 at the centre
of the unit box, cells=32^3, lmax=1, refine_to_sdf(band=3.0) — a FINEST-BAND mesh; mu=0.1,
f=1e-3, dt=60, advection off, 400 steps; reference = the same sphere on a uniform 32^3, lmax=0):

  uniform-fine reference          k = 1.0101549502e-01   (32768 leaves)
  graded band=3.0, cf=0           k = 9.8016614805e-02   rel err 2.968733e-02
  graded band=3.0, cf=1           k = 1.0147871218e-01   rel err 4.585605e-03

BIT-IDENTICAL, digit for digit, in both arms. NB these absolutes do not reproduce the
5.15e-02 -> 1.22e-02 pair quoted in ROADMAP §A6 and in the design note's gate P; that measurement's
exact recipe was never recorded, so this file pins one. What the gate asserts — that a finest-band
mesh does not move — holds.


