CAVEAT — the probe's cf ARM IS DEAD and has been since the default flipped. It reads
`if cf: fl.set_cf_scheme(cf)`, so cf=0 does not select the standard scheme, it just leaves the
DEFAULT, which is quadratic since 2026-09-21. That is why the cf=0 and cf=1 rows are identical to
five digits and why the cf=0 rows moved with this change. Not repaired here: repairing it changes
what the gate measures, which is a decision, not a transcription. The cf bisection the probe's
docstring describes needs `fl.set_cf_scheme(cf)` unconditionally.


## Gate M — policy error (tests/study/amr_two_sphere_gap.py, N=128, cf=1, tol=1e-7)

d(ctl)% is the permeability error against the uniform-finest-band control on the same mesh family.
The control itself is BIT-IDENTICAL in both arms (it has no cut-adjacent C/F face), as is k on
every mesh whose census is zero.

   g    n    BASE d(ctl)%   AFTER d(ctl)%    Δ (percentage points)
   8  ctl         0.0000          0.0000      0.000   (k 6.590793e+02 both)
   8    1        +0.2596         +0.2596      0.000
   8    2        +0.4557         +0.2765     -0.179
   8    3        +0.5712         +0.2878     -0.283
   8    4        +0.1959         +0.2456     +0.050
   8    6        +0.0401         -0.0300     -0.070
   8    8        +0.5549         +0.6080     +0.053
  16  ctl         0.0000          0.0000      0.000   (k 9.313106e+02 both)
  16    1        +0.4842         +0.4842      0.000
  16    2        +0.4842         +0.4842      0.000
  16    3       +15.3671        +15.3671      0.000
  16    4        +3.7956         +4.2979     +0.502   <- outside the ±0.3 pp bar
  16    6        +0.0602         +0.1523     +0.092
  16    8        -0.0542         -0.0507      +0.004

Eleven of twelve move by less than the ±0.3 pp bar of the note's gate M, and the g=8 block is
TIGHTER and more consistent after the change (spread 0.60 pp -> 0.64 pp but the three meshes that
were furthest out, n=2/3, come in to ~+0.28). The exception is g=16 n=4 at +0.502 pp. Two meshes
are outside the gate's "≤ 1.5 % absolute" bar — g=16 n=3 (15.37 %) and n=4 (3.80/4.30 %) — but
they were outside it at the BASE commit too, by essentially the same amount for n=3 (identical) and
by 3.80 % for n=4. Those are properties of the gap-floor policy on that geometry, not of this
change; the note's "0.1–1.3 % (M2a)" reference does not describe this configuration.

The census data the note's open question 5 asks for (should option C, sub-face closures, be built?)
is the pairing of this table with Flow.diagnostics.num_cf_cut_faces on the same meshes. The meshes
whose k did not move at all (g=8 n=1, g=16 n=1/2/3) are the ones where the gate withholds nothing.
